    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504">

                <pb facs="0481" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg469"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.91/11–444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-11-04T14:00:00+03:25">November 4, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:18 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>813. Further reports indicating change in Soviet attitude give increasingly
                    hopeful tinge to local picture.</p>
                <p>Iranian Chief of Staff says Russian restrictions on Iranian troops Tabriz have
                    been removed and situation there restored to <hi rendition="#italic">status quo
                        ante</hi>. He also states his reports indicate all quiet throughout Russian
                    zone. Soviet military here and Tabriz appear to be trying to explain, minimize
                    or disavow reported arbitrary actions of officer commanding at Tabriz and have
                    suggested formation of mixed Soviet and Iranian military commission to
                    investigate. (Purely Iranian mission to investigate recent events has either
                    left or is supposed about to leave for Tabriz.)</p>
                <p>Soviet railroad authorities today informed Cereals and Bread Section<anchor
                        n="85" xml:id="d504-f1"/> they had accepted proposed program for rail
                    movement of grain south to Tehran during November. If made in good faith this
                    statement means that ban imposed by Russians October 16 on civilian goods
                    transport to and from northern zone has been lifted.</p>
                <p>Unconfirmed report originating in Iranian Foreign Office says Kavtaradze has been
                    recalled to Moscow.</p>
                <p>Sent to Department repeated to Moscow and Tabriz.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
